      <PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>Use technology to spark civic innovation for social good</PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>KP Programs: Further development of 5 of the KP Civic Innovation Fellowship projects, along with continued support for select initiatives from previous Fellowship cycles, benefiting 191,000 users. The team also trained nearly 200 government staff, and provided mentorship to 20 interns from the KP Women's Civic Digital Internship Program. Under the Civic Innovator Program, 6 university student teams designed and developed 6 digital solutions for 5 government departments, promoting innovation and the use of civic technology to improve public service delivery and citizen engagement.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>0</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>91936</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>National projects: Trial work was undertaken on an electronic election management system by university students working on their final year project to build an electronic voting machine. Work was done on Paigham, a mass notification and SMS delivery platform that sends government alerts and announcements to citizens. Pehchaan, a single digital ID authentication system that acts as one login for multiple government services, was prototyped. Nizam, a design system for government websites, was created. Numainda, an AI chatbot for legal information, was launched.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>0</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>42377</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Community Engagement: Citizen engagement events to promote participation, collaboratively identify community challenges, and co-create solutions. This included a mapathon, Google Developer events, an event promoting environmental community cleanup, volunteer meetups, and hack days.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
